      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "JQ::Lite versions before 2.51 for Perl execute Perl code embedded in a query's regular expression by compiling it with string eval.\n\nThe pattern given to test(), match(), or the match and =~ conditions of select() is placed in a `qr'...'` literal and compiled as source text, so a `(?{ ... })` code block in it runs without `use re 'eval'`. Single quotes in the pattern are escaped, but a code block runs in place and needs none.\n\nAn attacker who supplies a query, or text that an application inserts into the pattern of one, can execute arbitrary Perl code in the calling process.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
